title: PLA
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Polylactic acid. A plastic made from plant sugars, usually corn or sugarcane, in place of oil.

It can be molded in the same machines as ordinary plastic.

It is compostable, with a catch. It needs the heat of an industrial composting facility. In a backyard pile or a landfill it mostly sits there.

It is not recyclable, at least not in the normal plastic recycling process. Put in with ordinary plastics it is a contaminant.

So it has one way back, and only where the right facility exists. In most places it fits neither bin. See [[Recyclable, but really?]]

Used in the [[Flax Chair]] and the [[Peel Chair]].

The [[Flax Chair]] is the exception that shows the rule. It was designed to be shredded and pressed again. That loop works because its maker set it up for that one product. It is not the same as a public recycling bin.
